# PR Squash Merge

Squash and merge a Pull Request with full status verification, conflict handling, and branch cleanup.

## Prerequisites

- `gh` CLI installed and authenticated
- PR number known (or detect from current branch)

## Verification Steps

```bash
gh pr view <pr-number> --json state,mergeable,mergeStateStatus
gh pr checks <pr-number>
gh pr review <pr-number> --list
```

## State Handling

| State | Action |
|-------|--------|
| OPEN + CLEAN | Proceed to merge |
| OPEN + CONFLICTING | Report conflicts, do not merge |
| OPEN + BEHIND | Update base branch, re-check |
| CLOSED | Report already closed |
| MERGED | Report already merged |

## Merge Command

```bash
gh pr merge <pr-number> --squash --delete-branch
```

## Post-Merge Cleanup

```bash
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git branch -D <branch>
```

## Error Labels

- Conflicts: `status/conflicts`
- CI failed: `ci/failed`
- Needs review: `status/needs-review`

## Output Format

```markdown
- pr_number: <number>
- pr_url: <url>
- branch: <branch>
- merge_commit: <hash>
- deleted_remote_branch: true/false
- deleted_local_branch: true/false
- warnings: [...]
- errors: [...]
```
